Logical Operator Description <code>&amp;&amp;</code> AND — both conditions must be true <code>\|\|</code> OR — at least one condition must be true <pre><code>let input: number = Number(prompt("Enter an odd number between 1 and 10: "));

if (input &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; input &lt;= 10 &amp;&amp; input % 2 !== 0) {
  console.log("Great! You entered an odd number between 1 and 10");
} else {
  console.log("That is not an odd number between 1 and 10");
}
</code></pre>
